 gy=[item('AU','Guzman y Gomez',s) for s in ['Burrito — Mild Grilled Chicken','Bowl — Mild Grilled Chicken','Caesar Burrito — Mild Grilled Chicken']]
 body='''<p>In Guzman y Gomez’s March 9, 2026 Australian guide, the standard mild grilled chicken burrito has <strong>773 kcal and 48.3 g protein</strong>; the mild grilled chicken bowl has <strong>659 kcal and 43.8 g protein</strong>. The bowl is 114 kcal lower and has 4.5 g less protein per listed order.</p><h2>The complete builds differ</h2>'''+table(gy,'Guzman y Gomez Australia: standard mild grilled chicken builds')+'''<p>The burrito is a listed 480 g serving and the bowl 455 g. Carbohydrate differs by 16.9 g, fat by 3 g and sodium by 250 mg. These are whole-build differences. Subtracting the bowl from the burrito does not measure one tortilla or guarantee the effect of “no wrap.”</p><h2>Caesar is another recipe</h2><p>The mild grilled chicken Caesar Burrito has 855 kcal, 44.8 g protein and 48.7 g fat. It shares the chicken description with the other two orders but has a different complete recipe. Do not attach the regular bowl’s values to it because both contain grilled chicken.</p><h2>Choose a comparison basis deliberately</h2><p>Listed serving answers “what would this order provide?” Equal weight answers a different density question and is only available when both source weights are supported. For the bowl, 659 ÷ 455 × 100 gives about 144.8 kcal per 100 g; for the regular burrito, 773 ÷ 480 × 100 gives about 161 kcal per 100 g. Those calculations do not describe a separately sold 100 g menu item.</p>'''+compare(gy[:2])+'''<p>Keep mild versus spicy, standard size, the Australian market and any extras explicit. This source edition is not a claim of the newest menu at every location, and the comparison does not infer extra chicken or guacamole portions.</p>'''
